# Gate step 1204-3s2s — data, not code.
#
# Binds the gate-step metrics isolation check. The guard itself lives in
# build.sh's step loop (it must, to observe each step); this fixture pins that
# the guard is there, that the subject fixture no longer reaches the host's log,
# and — the load-bearing part — that an unnamed run genuinely DOES split it.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FIXTURE RATHER THAN AN ARM IN test-metrics-log-path-agreement.sh,
# which is the natural home: that fixture is an ORPHAN (invoked by no gate step,
# no litmus binding, no build.sh call) and a prior adversarial orphan-disposition
# sweep classified it FIX_FIRST — "wiring it before the fix converts a latent
# library bug into an intermittent, misattributed gate failure". Putting this
# arm there would mean either leaving it unrun like the rest of that file, or
# binding a body that a second reader already refused to wire. Neither is a
# guard. This file is the bindable half; the agreement fixture stays the home
# for the PATH-AGREEMENT contract once its own blocker is cleared.
#
# THE ARM THAT MATTERS IS ARM 3, the negative control. Without it arm 2 passes
# in a world where nothing writes timing records at all, and the fixture would
# assert the absence of something that cannot happen. Its first draft did
# exactly that: a stripped copy in a temp dir resolved its own ROOT to /tmp,
# copied no scripts/, never reached the runner, and wrote nothing — passing the
# absence check for a reason with nothing to do with the subject.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a gate step cannot write into the host's shared metrics log (1204-3s2s)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-gate-step-metrics-isolation.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a gate step reached the host's shared metrics path (1204-3s2s) — one fixture writing /tmp/tillandsias-timing.jsonl splits the timing log, cycle-metrics then refuses every number, arms driving it read zero, and check-release-tier-freshness answers never:release-tier on this host from then on; see the failing arm above"
STEP_OK="gate-step metrics isolation check passed"
# Exit 3 means the subject fixture is absent — nothing was exercised, and the
# fixture says so by name rather than passing.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=3
STEP_SKIP_DESC="scripts/test-litmus-budget-tally.sh is absent, so the isolation could not be exercised"
